      {
        "id": 227758,
        "name": "Dandolo",
        "username": "Dandolo",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dandolo/{size}/1845_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-05T11:37:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MsbS\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/msbs/48/2056_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MsbS:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>OK, so I can feed into the big ‘stats data gathering’ via Google form, will I then be able to extract data for my plays only? As I’d be interested to know ‘I’ve not played against Ambuscade in ages’ or that ‘I’ve never defeated the Apostate with Haka on my team’.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, you’ll be able to view all your own stats under the Contributors section.</p>\n<p>Edit: Though it doesn’t get as specific as I’ve individual hero win rates against specific villains. If you’re looking for that type of data it’s probably worth just tracking your games yourself in a spreadsheet.</p>",
